{"id":"mahabharata-3-050","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":50,"title":"पञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 50 · Nala, Damayanti and the swan","summary":{"en":"Brihadashva tells of Nala, king of the Nishadhas, and Damayanti, the peerless princess of Vidarbha, who fall in love by hearing of each other. A golden swan whom Nala spares flies to Damayanti and praises Nala to her, and returns with her love.","kn":"ನಿಷಧರಾಜ ನಳ ಮತ್ತು ವಿದರ್ಭದ ಅಪ್ರತಿಮ ರಾಜಕುಮಾರಿ ದಮಯಂತಿ ಪರಸ್ಪರರ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಕೇಳಿಯೇ ಪ್ರೇಮಿಸುವ ಕಥೆಯನ್ನು ಬೃಹದಶ್ವರು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ನಳನು ಉಳಿಸಿದ ಚಿನ್ನದ ಹಂಸವು ದಮಯಂತಿಯಲ್ಲಿಗೆ ಹಾರಿ ನಳನನ್ನು ಹೊಗಳಿ ಅವಳ ಪ್ರೇಮದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಮರಳುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"बृहदश्व निषधराज नल और विदर्भ की अनुपम राजकुमारी दमयन्ती की कथा सुनाते हैं, जो एक-दूसरे के बारे में सुनकर ही प्रेम करने लगते हैं। नल द्वारा छोड़ा गया एक सुनहरा हंस दमयन्ती के पास उड़कर नल की प्रशंसा करता है और उसका प्रेम लेकर लौटता है।","te":"నిషధరాజు నలుడు, విదర్భ అప్రతిమ రాజకుమారి దమయంతి ఒకరి గురించి ఒకరు విని ప్రేమలో పడిన కథను బృహదశ్వుడు చెబుతాడు. నలుడు విడిచిపెట్టిన బంగారు హంస దమయంతి వద్దకు ఎగిరి నలుని కొనియాడి ఆమె ప్రేమతో తిరిగివస్తుంది.","ta":"நிஷத மன்னன் நளனும், விதர்ப நாட்டு ஒப்பற்ற இளவரசி தமயந்தியும் ஒருவரைப் பற்றி ஒருவர் கேட்டே காதலுற்ற கதையைப் ப்ருஹதஶ்வர் சொல்கிறார். நளன் உயிருடன் விட்ட பொன் அன்னம் தமயந்தியிடம் பறந்து நளனைப் புகழ்ந்து, அவள் காதலுடன் திரும்புகிறது.","ml":"നിഷധരാജാവായ നളനെയും വിദർഭയിലെ അതുല്യസുന്ദരിയായ രാജകുമാരി ദമയന്തിയെയും ബൃഹദശ്വൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു; ഇരുവരും പരസ്പരം കേട്ടറിഞ്ഞ് പ്രണയത്തിലാകുന്നു. നളൻ ദയവോടെ വിട്ടയച്ച ഒരു സ്വർണ്ണഹംസം ദമയന്തിയുടെ അടുത്ത് പറന്നെത്തി നളനെ പ്രശംസിക്കുന്നു; അവൾക്ക് നളനോട് സ്നേഹം ജനിക്കുന്നു, അവളുടെ സ്നേഹവുമായി ഹംസം മടങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.50; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"इन्द्रलोकाभिगमनपर्व","titleEn":"Indralokabhigamana Parva (Journey to Indra's world)","verses":[{"text":"बृहदश्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brihadashva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"आसीद्राजा नलो नाम वीरसेनसुतो बली ।\nउपपन्नो गुणैरिष्टै रूपवानश्वकोविदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was a king named Nala, the strong son of Virasena, endowed with desirable qualities, handsome and expert with horses."}},{"n":2,"text":"अतिष्ठन्मनुजेन्द्राणां मूर्ध्नि देवपतिर्यथा ।\nउपर्युपरि सर्वेषामादित्य इव तेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He stood at the head of the lords of men as the lord of gods does, above all others, like the sun in brilliance."}},{"n":3,"text":"ब्रह्मण्यो वेदविच्छूरो निषधेषु महीपतिः ।\nअक्षप्रियः सत्यवादी महानक्षौहिणीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devoted to brahmins, learned in the Vedas, brave, a ruler of the Nishadhas, fond of dice, truthful, he was lord of a great akshauhini."}},{"n":4,"text":"ईप्सितो वरनारीणामुदारः संयतेन्द्रियः ।\nरक्षिता धन्विनां श्रेष्ठः साक्षादिव मनुः स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Desired by the finest women, generous and self-controlled, he was the protector of the people and the best of archers, as if Manu himself."}},{"n":5,"text":"तथैवासीद्विदर्भेषु भीमो भीमपराक्रमः ।\nशूरः सर्वगुणैर्युक्तः प्रजाकामः स चाप्रजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise in Vidarbha there was Bhima, of fearsome prowess, brave and full of every virtue, who wanted children but had none."}},{"n":6,"text":"स प्रजार्थे परं यत्नमकरोत्सुसमाहितः ।\nतमभ्यगच्छद्ब्रह्मर्षिर्दमनो नाम भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"With full concentration he made great effort for offspring, and the brahmin sage named Damana came to him, descendant of Bharata."}},{"n":7,"text":"तं स भीमः प्रजाकामस्तोषयामास धर्मवित् ।\nमहिष्या सह राजेन्द्र सत्कारेण सुवर्चसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, who knew dharma and wanted offspring, pleased the radiant sage with honor, together with his queen, O king."}},{"n":8,"text":"तस्मै प्रसन्नो दमनः सभार्याय वरं ददौ ।\nकन्यारत्नं कुमारांश्च त्रीनुदारान्महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pleased, the greatly renowned Damana gave the couple a boon: a jewel of a daughter and three noble sons."}},{"n":9,"text":"दमयन्तीं दमं दान्तं दमनं च सुवर्चसम् ।\nउपपन्नान्गुणैः सर्वैर्भीमान्भीमपराक्रमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were Damayanti, Dama, Danta and the radiant Damana, all endowed with every quality and terrible in might like their father."}},{"n":10,"text":"दमयन्ती तु रूपेण तेजसा यशसा श्रिया ।\nसौभाग्येन च लोकेषु यशः प्राप सुमध्यमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Damayanti, slender-waisted, won fame in the worlds for her beauty, splendor, renown, grace and good fortune."}},{"n":11,"text":"अथ तां वयसि प्राप्ते दासीनां समलंकृतम् ।\nशतं सखीनां च तथा पर्युपास्ते शचीमिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"When she came of age, a hundred adorned maidservants and a hundred friends attended her, as they do Shachi."}},{"n":12,"text":"तत्र स्म भ्राजते भैमी सर्वाभरणभूषिता ।\nसखीमध्येऽनवद्याङ्गी विद्युत्सौदामिनी यथा ।\nअतीव रूपसंपन्ना श्रीरिवायतलोचना ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Bhima's daughter shone, decked in all ornaments, faultless in limb among her friends like a flash of lightning, utterly beautiful, large-eyed like Shri herself."}},{"n":13,"text":"न देवेषु न यक्षेषु तादृग्रूपवती क्वचित् ।\nमानुषेष्वपि चान्येषु दृष्टपूर्वा न च श्रुता ।\nचित्तप्रमाथिनी बाला देवानामपि सुन्दरी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such beauty was never seen or heard of among gods or yakshas, or other humans; that young girl, lovely even to the gods, unsettled every heart."}},{"n":14,"text":"नलश्च नरशार्दूलो रूपेणाप्रतिमो भुवि ।\nकन्दर्प इव रूपेण मूर्तिमानभवत्स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Nala, tiger among men, was unmatched on earth in beauty, as if Kandarpa himself had taken form."}},{"n":15,"text":"तस्याः समीपे तु नलं प्रशशंसुः कुतूहलात् ।\nनैषधस्य समीपे तु दमयन्तीं पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Out of curiosity people praised Nala to her, and praised Damayanti again and again to the Nishadha king."}},{"n":16,"text":"तयोरदृष्टकामोऽभूच्छृण्वतोः सततं गुणान् ।\nअन्योन्यं प्रति कौन्तेय स व्यवर्धत हृच्छयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing each other's virtues unceasingly, they grew in love for one another, though they had not seen each other, Kaunteya. That desire in the heart increased."}},{"n":17,"text":"अशक्नुवन्नलः कामं तदा धारयितुं हृदा ।\nअन्तःपुरसमीपस्थे वन आस्ते रहोगतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unable then to hold back his desire in his heart, Nala sat in a forest near the women's quarters, alone."}},{"n":18,"text":"स ददर्श तदा हंसाञ्जातरूपपरिच्छदान् ।\nवने विचरतां तेषामेकं जग्राह पक्षिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he saw swans with golden plumage, and as they roamed in the forest he caught one of the birds."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततोऽन्तरिक्षगो वाचं व्याजहार तदा नलम् ।\nन हन्तव्योऽस्मि ते राजन्करिष्यामि हि ते प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the bird, moving through the sky, spoke to Nala: \"You should not kill me, king, for I will do you a kindness."}},{"n":20,"text":"दमयन्तीसकाशे त्वां कथयिष्यामि नैषध ।\nयथा त्वदन्यं पुरुषं न सा मंस्यति कर्हिचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will speak of you before Damayanti, Nishadha, so that she will never think of any man other than you.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"एवमुक्तस्ततो हंसमुत्ससर्ज महीपतिः ।\nते तु हंसाः समुत्पत्य विदर्भानगमंस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told this, the king let the swan go. The swans flew up and went to Vidarbha."}},{"n":22,"text":"विदर्भनगरीं गत्वा दमयन्त्यास्तदान्तिके ।\nनिपेतुस्ते गरुत्मन्तः सा ददर्शाथ तान्खगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the city of Vidarbha, those winged birds alighted near Damayanti, and she saw them."}},{"n":23,"text":"सा तानद्भुतरूपान्वै दृष्ट्वा सखिगणावृता ।\nहृष्टा ग्रहीतुं खगमांस्त्वरमाणोपचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those wonderfully formed birds, surrounded by her group of friends, she was delighted and hurried to catch them."}},{"n":24,"text":"अथ हंसा विससृपुः सर्वतः प्रमदावने ।\nएकैकशस्ततः कन्यास्तान्हंसान्समुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the swans scattered everywhere in the pleasure grove, and the girls ran after the swans one by one."}},{"n":25,"text":"दमयन्ती तु यं हंसं समुपाधावदन्तिके ।\nस मानुषीं गिरं कृत्वा दमयन्तीमथाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The swan that Damayanti ran after came near and, speaking in human speech, said to her:"}},{"n":26,"text":"दमयन्ति नलो नाम निषधेषु महीपतिः ।\nअश्विनोः सदृशो रूपे न समास्तस्य मानुषाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Damayanti, in Nishadha there is a king named Nala. He resembles the Ashvins in beauty; no human can equal him."}},{"n":27,"text":"तस्य वै यदि भार्या त्वं भवेथा वरवर्णिनि ।\nसफलं ते भवेज्जन्म रूपं चेदं सुमध्यमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you would be his wife, fair-complexioned lady, your birth and this beauty of yours, slender-waisted one, would be fulfilled."}},{"n":28,"text":"वयं हि देवगन्धर्वमनुष्योरगराक्षसान् ।\nदृष्टवन्तो न चास्माभिर्दृष्टपूर्वस्तथाविधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have seen gods, gandharvas, humans, nagas and rakshasas, and have never seen the like of him."}},{"n":29,"text":"त्वं चापि रत्नं नारीणां नरेषु च नलो वरः ।\nविशिष्टाया विशिष्टेन संगमो गुणवान्भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the jewel among women and Nala the best among men. The union of the best with the best would be of great worth.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"एवमुक्ता तु हंसेन दमयन्ती विशां पते ।\nअब्रवीत्तत्र तं हंसं तमप्येवं नलं वद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to thus by the swan, Damayanti, lord of people, said to it: \"Tell Nala the same.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"तथेत्युक्त्वाण्डजः कन्यां वैदर्भस्य विशां पते ।\nपुनरागम्य निषधान्नले सर्वं न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"So be it,\" the egg-born bird returned from Vidarbha's princess to Nishadha and told Nala everything."}}]}]}